<title>JAPAN: Moody's assigns Aa1 to Kyushu Electric bonds.</title>
<headline>Moody's assigns Aa1 to Kyushu Electric bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Monday it had assigned its Aa1 rating to Kyushu Electric Power Co Inc's offering of 350 million Swiss francs worth of 4.00 percent bonds due 2007.</p>
<p>The rating is based on Kyushu Electric Power's importance to the local economy, its crucial role as a supplier within the Japanese utility industry and its very favourable industry operating environment, Moody's said in a statement.</p>
</text>
